  "parsing_res_list": [
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "When someone is giving advice in order to make themselves feel more powerful, there is underlying anxiety to their behavior that recipients of the advice tend to notice. It can be tempting in this situation to react harshly to the advice given and to accuse them of being manipulative, but this approach might produce an undesirable result.",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        76,
        1124,
        165
      ],
      "block_id": 0,
      "block_order": 1,
      "group_id": 0,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          76.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          76.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          165.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          165.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "If the act of giving advice is contributing actively to someone's feelings of self-worth, an outright (直率的) rejection may be perceived as a threat, activating their fight-or-flight response, possibly causing them to double down on their validation-seeking behavior, or leading to a larger conflict.",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        170,
        1125,
        258
      ],
      "block_id": 1,
      "block_order": 2,
      "group_id": 1,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          170.0
        ],
        [
          1125.0,
          170.0
        ],
        [
          1125.0,
          258.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          258.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "The key is to validate without over-identifying. You can let them know that you have heard them and appreciate where they are coming from without taking on the potentially damaging narrative that you could not have gotten by without their help. You had better say something like, “Thanks for the idea. I have my own plan for handling this, but I really appreciate your perspective and will take it into consideration. Can I let you know when I need help in the future?”",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        265,
        1124,
        384
      ],
      "block_id": 2,
      "block_order": 3,
      "group_id": 2,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          265.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          265.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          384.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          384.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "If you have trouble setting boundaries tactfully, prioritize working on your own ability to self-regulate. As uncomfortable as it may make you continuously receiving unwanted advice, if you can respond with compassion, the situation will likely diffuse much faster.",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        388,
        1124,
        476
      ],
      "block_id": 3,
      "block_order": 4,
      "group_id": 3,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          388.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          388.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          476.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          476.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Though it is usually not the intended outcome of giving unsolicited advice, many who receive it often feel stressed, offended, or simply annoyed by unwanted suggestions. Setting a boundary in this regard, if you feel you need one, is perfectly reasonable and something that can bring you increased emotional safety.",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        482,
        1124,
        570
      ],
      "block_id": 4,
      "block_order": 5,
      "group_id": 4,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          482.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          482.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          570.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          570.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "It is best to set boundaries in a way that takes into account the individual's underlying reasons for doing what they are doing to avoid unnecessary conflict and more stress.",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        577,
        1124,
        634
      ],
      "block_id": 5,
      "block_order": 6,
      "group_id": 5,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          67.0,
          577.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          577.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          634.0
        ],
        [
          67.0,
          634.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "51. What is the finding of one study about people who keep giving unsolicited advice?\nA) They turn out to be well-meaning. C) They are capable of influencing others.\nB) They are genuinely kind-hearted. D) They are inclined to crave for power.",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        670,
        933,
        758
      ],
      "block_id": 6,
      "block_order": 7,
      "group_id": 6,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          67.0,
          670.0
        ],
        [
          933.0,
          670.0
        ],
        [
          933.0,
          758.0
        ],
        [
          67.0,
          758.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "52. What is the problem with people who are driven to give you unsolicited advice?\nA) They may be quick to upset others. C) They want their voice to be the loudest.\nB) They may be emotionally vulnerable. D) They respond to discomfort excessively.",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        765,
        944,
        851
      ],
      "block_id": 7,
      "block_order": 8,
      "group_id": 7,
      "block_polygon_points": [
